class:: ModalReverbModel
summary:: Prepared frequencies, decays, residues, and phases for a modal space
categories:: UGens>Reverbs, Libraries>CamaraObscura
related:: Guides/CamaraObscura, Classes/ModalReverbBank

description::

ModalReverbModel stores up to 4096 damped complex modes. Each row contains
frequency, amplitude T60, input residue, stereo output residues, and phase.
Models can be deliberately random or harmonic, supplied explicitly, or
extracted from integer-PCM WAV by the bundled dependency-free
code::modal_extract:: tool.

The extractor uses refined Hann-window FFT peaks and a two-band Schroeder
decay estimate. It is a transparent compact approximation, not ESPRIT or a
matrix-pencil estimator. The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/DynKlank::;
ModalReverbBank adds per-mode decay metadata, stereo residues, phase, stable
freeze, and prepared models suited to much larger banks.

classmethods::

method:: fromModes
Create a model from parallel mode arrays.

argument:: frequencies
Positive modal frequencies below the inferred model Nyquist frequency.

argument:: decays
Positive amplitude T60 seconds.

argument:: gains
Scalar gains or stereo gain pairs.

argument:: sampleRate
Model sample rate in hertz. Frequencies must remain below its Nyquist
frequency, and the loaded model must match the server sample rate.

method:: fromIR
Synchronously run the installed code::modal_extract.py:: tool on integer-PCM
WAV and read its temporary model.

argument:: path
WAV path.

argument:: modes
Requested peak count from 1 through 4096.

method:: fromAnalysis
Read a model already produced by the external tool.

method:: random
Create logarithmically distributed deterministic frequencies and decays.

method:: harmonic
Create integer harmonics below Nyquist.

method:: read
Read a version-1 modal model.

instancemethods::

method:: validate
Validate metadata plus every modal frequency, decay, residue, and phase.

method:: summary
Return concise diagnostics.

method:: load
Upload to a mono Buffer.

method:: write
Serialize the model.

method:: free
Free the last uploaded Buffer.

method:: plotModes
Plot modal frequencies.

method:: plotDecay
Plot modal T60 values.

examples::

code::
(
var model = ModalReverbModel.random(
    512, [70, 15000], [0.4, 5],
    seed: 12, sampleRate: 48000
);
model.summary.postln;
model.plotModes;
)
::

code::
(
var model = ModalReverbModel.harmonic(
    55, 128, 4, sampleRate: 48000
);
model.validate;
model.plotDecay;
)
::

